
=== H2

The H2 database allows only Java-based triggers. Therefore the H2 dialect requires that the SymmetricDS jar file be in the database's classpath.

A file-based H2 database can use either the `file:` or the `async:` file system prefix.
Both use the same database file and format, so an existing database opens unchanged after the prefix is switched.

* `file:` (default) reads and writes through a Java NIO `FileChannel`. If a thread is interrupted during file I/O, Java closes the channel and H2 marks the database closed, so later statements fail until the engine restarts.
* `async:`, for example `db.url=jdbc:h2:async:./corp;LOCK_TIMEOUT=60000;WRITE_DELAY=0`, uses an `AsynchronousFileChannel`, which stays open when a thread is interrupted. On Linux, Java runs every read through a thread pool, which made H2 processing about 15 to 45 percent slower in replication tests. Use it only when the database is closed by interrupted threads, reported as `ClosedByInterruptException` or `Database is already closed`.

.Supported Data Types
|===
|Data Type|Supported?

|Int, TinyInt, SmallInt, BigInt|Yes
|Boolean|Yes
|Decimal|Yes
|Double, Real|Yes
|Time, Date, Timestamp|Yes
|Binary, Blob|Yes
|===
